# GET /catalog/sha256:<hex>: one object by its content address
route     GET /catalog/sha256:<hex>
handler   object
memo      the contract of GET /catalog/sha256:<hex> on tiesapi.com
input
  <hex>: 64 lowercase hex, the sha256 of the bytes wanted
processing
  1 refuse anything that is not 64 hex
  2 read catalog/objects/<hex> if its bytes hash to <hex>; else a named entry whose sha256 is <hex>
  3 take the abstract: the title, and which of input, processing, output, graph the text has
output
  200 {id, url, sha256, bytes, title, parts}; 404 when no bytes are here: the address is still a valid label
  check: sha256 of bytes equals id
graph
  builds on catalog-entry
  the id exists before any name is assigned, so a register line may carry it as its label at once
example
  GET /catalog/sha256:d88a5318c032335902db7e50d608e35a49a1d15922bdaafdb01f79e45b4b910c
